(8775,'What is a book?','','none'),
(8776,'A book is a structured group of content pages, arranged in a hierarchical structure called a <em>book outline</em>. A book hierarchy can be up to nine levels deep, and a book can include <em>Book page</em> content items or other content items. Every book has a default book-specific navigation block, which contains links that lead to the previous and next pages in the book and to the level above the current page in the book\'s structure.','','none'),
(8777,'What are the permissions for books?','','none'),
(8778,'Allows users to add new books to the site.','','none'),
(8779,'Add content and child pages to books and manage their hierarchies','','none'),
(8780,'Allows users to add configured types of content to existing books.','','none'),
(8781,'Allows users to add <em>any</em> type of content to a book, use the book overview administration page, and rearrange the pages of a book from the book outline page.','','none'),
(8782,'Administer site configuration (in the System module section)','','none'),
(8783,'Allows users to do many site configuration tasks, including configuring books. This permission has security implications.','','none'),
(8784,'Allows users to click the <em>printer-friendly version</em> link to generate a printer-friendly display of the page, which includes pages below it in the book outline.','','none'),
(8785,'<em>Book page</em> content permissions (in the Node module section)','','none'),
(8786,'Like other content types, the <em>Book page</em> content type has separate permissions for creating, editing, and deleting a user\'s own and any content items of this type.','','none'),
