(8871,'Manage the search index, and make sure that the site is fully indexed for searching.','','10.4.0'),
(8872,'What is the search index?','','10.4.0'),
(8873,'Under <em>Indexing throttle</em>, select the <em>Number of items to index per cron run</em>. A smaller number will make cron faster and reduce the possibility of timeout; a larger number will make sure more of your site is indexed in fewer cron runs.','','10.4.0'),
(8874,'Under <em>Default indexing settings</em>, enter the desired <em>Minimum word length to index</em>. Words smaller than this length will be dropped from both keywords when searching and content when indexing.','','10.4.0'),
(8875,'If your site uses Chinese, Japanese, or Korean languages, optionally check <em>Simple CJK handling</em> under <em>Default indexing settings</em> to provide some support for these languages.','','10.4.0'),
(8876,'Click <em>Save configuration</em>, and you should be returned to the <em>Search pages</em> page.','','10.4.0'),
(8877,'Click <em>Re-index site</em> if you have changed the indexing configuration, or later on, if you believe that the search index has been corrupted.','','10.4.0'),
(8878,'After waiting for cron to run several times, verify that the content has been fully indexed for searching. The overall status is listed under <em>Indexing progress</em>, and the status for each search page is shown in the <em>Indexing progress</em> column of the <em>Search pages</em> section.','','10.4.0'),
(8879,'What are search pages?','','10.4.0'),
(8880,'The core Search module organizes site search into <em>pages</em>. Each page allows users to search a particular type of content with a particular configuration. The configuration includes specifying a URL that starts with <em>search</em>, a name for the page, and additional options for some search page types.','','10.4.0'),
(8881,'What modules provide site search?','','10.4.0'),
(8882,'The core Search module provides the ability to configure search pages; search page types are provided by both core and contributed modules. The core modules that provide search page types are:','','10.4.0'),
(8883,'The Node module, for searching content pages','','10.4.0'),
(8884,'The User module, for searching user profiles','','10.4.0'),
(8885,'The Help module, for searching help topics','','10.4.0'),
(8886,'As an alternative to the core Search module\'s system of search pages, you can use contributed modules to provide site search. For example, the <a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/project/apachesolr\">Apache Solr</a> and <a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/project/sphinx\">Sphinx</a> contributed modules use third-party technology to provide site search.','','10.4.0'),
(8887,'What are the limitations of the core Search module?','','10.4.0'),
(8888,'There are two main limitations of the core Search module. First, it is not appropriate for very large sites -- if you have a large site, look into other search technologies like Apache Solr. Second, the Node search page type only supports exact keyword matching, which is not the behavior that most users will expect. You can improve this by installing a language-specific stemming module for your language (such as <a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/project/porterstemmer\">Porter Stemmer</a> for American English), which makes it so that, for example, a search for the word walk would match pages containing the words walk, walking, and walked.','','10.4.0'),
(8889,'What are the search permissions?','','10.4.0'),
(8890,'Users with <em>Use search</em> permission can use the <em>Search form</em> block and <em>Search</em> page; this permission is required for any search configured in the core Search module.','','10.4.0'),
(8891,'In addition to <em>Use search</em>, <em>View user information</em> permission is needed for searching users.','','10.4.0'),
(8892,'In addition to <em>Use search</em>, <em>View published content</em> permission is needed for searching content.','','10.4.0'),
(8893,'Users with <em>Use advanced search</em> permission can use more complex search filtering when performing content searches.','','10.4.0'),
(8894,'Configuring site search overview','','10.4.0'),
(8895,'<a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/documentation/modules/search\">Online documentation for the Search module</a>','','10.4.0'),
