(9072,'Verify that the order of links is correct. If it is not, drag menu links until the order is correct, and click <em>Save</em>.','','10.4.0'),
(9073,'Creating a menu','','10.4.0'),
(9074,'Create a new menu.','','10.4.0'),
(9075,'Click <em>Add menu</em>.','','10.4.0'),
(9076,'Enter the title for the menu, which is used as the default block title if the menu is displayed as a block. If desired, also edit the machine name of the menu, which is by default derived from the title.','','10.4.0'),
(9077,'Enter an administrative summary, which is displayed on the <em>Menus</em> page.','','10.4.0'),
(9078,'If your site has more than one language, choose the language for the menu.','','10.4.0'),
(9079,'Click <em>Save</em>. You will be on the menu editing page, ready to add links to the menu if the core Custom Menu Links module is installed; see related topics for further tasks.','','10.4.0'),
(9080,'Reordering and disabling menu links','','10.4.0'),
(9081,'Disable menu links or change the order and hierarchy of menu links.','','10.4.0'),
(9082,'Click <em>Edit menu</em> for the menu that you want to edit.','','10.4.0'),
(9083,'Drag menu links into a new order, or check/uncheck <em>Enabled</em> to enable or disable menu links.','','10.4.0'),
(9084,'Click <em>Save</em> to save your changes.','','10.4.0'),
(9085,'<a href=\"https://www.php.net/manual/datetime.format.php#refsect1-datetime.format-parameters\">PHP date format codes reference</a>','','10.4.0'),
(9086,'[site:name]: The name of your website.','','10.4.0'),
(9087,'[site:url]: The URL of your website.','','10.4.0'),
(9088,'Managing content listings (views)','','10.4.0'),
(9089,'What is a view?','','10.4.0'),
(9090,'A <em>view</em> is a listing of items on your site; for example, a block showing the most recent comments, a page listing news items, or a list of registered users. The listings can be formatted in a table, grid, list, calendar, RSS feed, and other formats (some output formats may require you to install additional contributed modules).','','10.4.0'),
(9091,'What are the components of a view?','','10.4.0'),
(9092,'When you first create a view, you will specify what type of <em>base data</em> is being displayed in the view, which cannot be changed. After choosing a base data type, you can edit the following components, which allow you to specify which data to output, in what order, and in what format:','','10.4.0'),
(9093,'<em>Displays</em>: whether the output goes to a page, block, feed, etc.; a single view can have multiple displays, each with different settings.','','10.4.0'),
(9094,'<em>Format</em>: the output style for each display, such as content item, grid, table, or HTML list.','','10.4.0'),
(9095,'<em>Fields</em>: if the Format allows, the particular fields to display.','','10.4.0'),
(9096,'<em>Filter criteria</em>: criteria to limit the data to output, such as whether the content is published, the type of content, etc. Filters can be <em>exposed</em> to let users choose how to filter the data.','','10.4.0'),
(9097,'<em>Sort criteria</em>: how to order the data. Sorting can also be exposed to users.','','10.4.0'),
(9098,'<em>Header</em> and <em>Footer</em>: content to display at the top or bottom of the view display.','','10.4.0'),
(9099,'<em>No results behavior</em>: what to do if the filter criteria result in having no data to display.','','10.4.0'),
(9100,'<em>Pager</em>: how many items to display, and how to paginate if there are additional items to display.','','10.4.0'),
(9101,'<em>Advanced</em> &gt; <em>Contextual filters</em>: like regular filters, except the criteria come from the <em>context</em>, such as the current date, page the view is displayed on, etc.','','10.4.0'),
(9102,'<em>Advanced</em> &gt; <em>Relationships</em>: additional data to pull in and display, related in some way to the base data of the view (such as data about the user who created the content item).','','10.4.0'),
